      "hints": [
        "Set $y = \\frac{2x}{3x - 1} \\implies 3xy - y = 2x \\implies x(3y - 2) = y$.",
        "Solve for $x = \\frac{y}{3y - 2}$ and state $f^{-1}(x) = \\frac{x}{3x - 2}$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Set $y = \\frac{2x}{3x - 1}$ and cross-multiply to isolate $x$:\n$$y(3x - 1) = 2x \\implies 3xy - y = 2x$$\n$$3xy - 2x = y \\implies x(3y - 2) = y$$\n$$x = \\frac{y}{3y - 2}$$",
        "Write down the inverse function in terms of $x$:\n$$f^{-1}(x) = \\frac{x}{3x - 2}$$"
      ],
